[?1049h[24;1H[?1h=# 0036 The C port[m
[m
Status: accepted 2026-10-16. The port is under way. Until its cutover,[m
the JavaScript app of decision 0001 is still the app.[m
[m
## Context[m
[m
The maintainer asked for skindeep to be rewritten in C, with standard[m
libraries, on Linux and macOS, with no Python and no JavaScript run. A[m
review put the work at about 79,000–106,000 lines of C. Most of it is[m
the platform beneath the app, which Chromium, xterm.js, node-pty and[m
butterchurn supply today.[m
[m
## Decision[m
[m
- Shared code is ISO C17 and POSIX.1-2008 with its XSI option[m
  (`_XOPEN_SOURCE=700`, which the pty functions need), and nothing[m
  else. Code for one operating system lives under[m
  `src/platform/<os>/`.[m
- Linux and macOS. On Linux the app speaks the X11 wire protocol over a[m
  socket, without Xlib; Wayland desktops run it under XWayland. On[m
  macOS it uses Apple's system frameworks only (AppKit, CoreGraphics,[m
  AudioToolbox, libproc, sysctl), called from C through the Objective-C[m
[7mdocs/decisions/0036-c-port.md[27m[K[K  runtime. XQuartz is never used.[m
- Three programs. `skinned` is the app. `skinned-relay` replaces[m
  `app/relay/hook.py` and `app/relay/statusline.js`. `skinc` compiles a[m
  skin into a pack.[m
- Skins stay `skin.json` plus `skin.css`. `skinc` resolves the CSS once,[m
  for every state a widget can reach. It pre-renders the static layers[m
  at 1x and 2x and decodes the images and sounds. The app composites[m
  packs and never interprets CSS. The four shipped skins are compiled[m
  during the build and linked in as generated C arrays. A skin passed[m
  with `--skin` is compiled when it first loads, then cached.[m
- Vendored code: single-file libraries whose licence is free to use[m
  (public domain or the Unlicense, MIT, BSD, ISC, zlib). Each lives in[m
  `third_party/<library>/` beside its licence and is listed in[m
  `ASSETS.json` (decision 0017). Today these are stb_truetype,[m
  stb_image, stb_vorbis, nanosvg, nanosvgrast and qoi.[m
  - stb_truetype does no range checking, so it reads only the embedded[m
    fonts, the system's fonts, and skin fonts `skinc` has checked.[m
  - `skinc` accepts only TrueType outlines in skins.[m
- HTTPS goes through the `curl` command, run as a child. libcurl is not[m
  linked, because its licence is curl's own, not MIT.[m
- No Python and no JavaScript in the C tree, its build or its tests. The[m
  fake CLIs and the live checks are rewritten in C or POSIX sh.[m
- The build is `make` with the system C compiler. The makefile uses only[m
